  "id": "bbdf6c82-2639-432c-a955-ea17159fdc0b",
  "title": "Annotation-Free Furniture Codes: Encoding and Transfer Across Different Asset Libraries",
  "summary": "Annotation-free furniture codes encode geometric object properties and enable transfer between asset libraries, leveraging self-supervised tokens derived from object geometry. These codes demonstrate robustness in recovering fine- and super-category information while adapting to varying alignment requirements.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "A Finite Scalar Quantization (FSQ) point-cloud autoencoder decouples furniture object encoding from 3D-FUTURE data, achieving 62.6% fine-category recovery.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Diagnostic probes reveal yaw signal recovery from codes, showing rotation content can be set by training objectives.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Scaling across ShapeNet datasets highlights category-dependent alignment for organically-shaped furniture.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
